<div class="alert alert-info">
  <div>
    Server-side Plunk sync only needs the secret API key and API base URL. Hosted and self-hosted Plunk are both supported,
    and the connection check verifies that Spree can reach the Plunk <code>/contacts</code> API with the supplied secret key.
  </div>
</div>

<div class="card mb-4">
  <div class="card-body">
    <h3 class="h6 mb-3">Core connection settings</h3>

    <%= preference_field(
      @integration,
      form,
      "plunk_base_url",
      i18n_scope: "admin.integrations.plunk",
    ) %>
    <p class="mb-4 mt-n2">
      Use the API base URL only, such as <code>https://next-api.useplunk.com</code> or
      <code>https://plunk.example.com/api</code>. Do not paste a specific endpoint like
      <code>/contacts</code>, <code>/events/track</code>, or <code>/v1/track</code>.
    </p>

    <%= preference_field(
      @integration,
      form,
      "plunk_secret_api_key",
      i18n_scope: "admin.integrations.plunk",
    ) unless @integration.new_record? %>
    <%= render(
      "spree/admin/integrations/forms/plunk_password_field",
      form: form,
      field: :preferred_plunk_secret_api_key,
      label: Spree.t("plunk_secret_api_key", scope: "admin.integrations.plunk"),
      required: true
    ) if @integration.new_record? %>
    <p class="mb-0 mt-n2">
      Required for server-side contact upserts and event tracking. Paste a Plunk secret server key for this workspace;
      public or browser-side keys will fail the connection test.
    </p>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="card mb-4">
  <div class="card-body">
    <h3 class="h6 mb-3">Optional sender defaults</h3>

    <%= preference_field(
      @integration,
      form,
      "default_from_email",
      i18n_scope: "admin.integrations.plunk",
    ) %>
    <p class="mb-4 mt-n2">
      Optional. Use a single mailbox such as <code>marketing@example.com</code>. Direct transactional sends through
      <code>/v1/send</code> require this mailbox's domain to be added and verified in Plunk. If left blank,
      <code>spree_plunk</code> falls back to the store mail-from address.
    </p>

    <%= preference_field(
      @integration,
      form,
      "default_from_name",
      i18n_scope: "admin.integrations.plunk",
    ) %>
    <p class="mb-0 mt-n2">
      Optional display name such as <code>Example Store</code>. If you set a sender name, also set a sender email so the
      stored sender identity stays complete.
    </p>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="card mb-4">
  <div class="card-body">
    <h3 class="h6 mb-3">Transactional email handoff</h3>

    <div class="alert alert-warning mt-n1">
      Default off. Enable these only when Plunk should send the selected transactional emails through
      <code>/v1/send</code>. Keep each email type owned by one sender to avoid duplicates while Spree mailers are still active.
      Localhost storefront URLs are fine for link generation during development, but the sender email domain must still be
      verified in Plunk.
    </div>

    <%= preference_field(
      @integration,
      form,
      "transactional_email_enabled",
      i18n_scope: "admin.integrations.plunk",
    ) %>
    <p class="mb-4 mt-n2">
      Master switch for direct Plunk transactional sends from this integration.
    </p>

    <%= preference_field(
      @integration,
      form,
      "password_reset_email_enabled",
      i18n_scope: "admin.integrations.plunk",
    ) %>
    <%= preference_field(
      @integration,
      form,
      "password_reset_template_id",
      i18n_scope: "admin.integrations.plunk",
    ) %>
    <p class="mb-4 mt-n2">
      Sends Store API password reset requests from <code>customer.password_reset_requested</code>. Tokens and reset URLs are
      passed as non-persistent Plunk data.
    </p>

    <%= preference_field(
      @integration,
      form,
      "newsletter_confirmation_email_enabled",
      i18n_scope: "admin.integrations.plunk",
    ) %>
    <%= preference_field(
      @integration,
      form,
      "newsletter_confirmation_template_id",
      i18n_scope: "admin.integrations.plunk",
    ) %>
    <p class="mb-4 mt-n2">
      Sends newsletter double opt-in confirmation from <code>newsletter_subscriber.subscription_requested</code>. This does
      not subscribe the contact in Plunk; Spree verification remains the consent source of truth.
    </p>

    <%= preference_field(
      @integration,
      form,
      "order_confirmation_resend_email_enabled",
      i18n_scope: "admin.integrations.plunk",
    ) %>
    <%= preference_field(
      @integration,
      form,
      "order_confirmation_template_id",
      i18n_scope: "admin.integrations.plunk",
    ) %>
    <p class="mb-0 mt-n2">
      Sends explicit order confirmation resends from <code>order.resend_confirmation_email</code>. Checkout-completion order
      receipts remain with Spree mailers until they get their own tested handoff.
    </p>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="card mb-4">
  <div class="card-body">
    <h3 class="h6 mb-3">Advanced</h3>

    <div class="alert alert-secondary mt-n1">
      The Public API Key is optional and intentionally unused by the current server-side MVP. Leave it blank unless you
      are preparing a later storefront or browser-side integration.
    </div>

    <div class="mt-3">
      <%= preference_field(
        @integration,
        form,
        "plunk_public_api_key",
        i18n_scope: "admin.integrations.plunk",
      ) %>
    </div>
    <p class="mb-0 mt-n2">
      Storing a Public API Key here does not enable client-side tracking on its own.
    </p>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="card mb-4">
  <div class="card-body">
    <h3 class="h6 mb-3">Inbound subscription-state webhook</h3>
    <% unsubscribe_webhook_path = @integration.persisted? ? plunk_unsubscribe_webhook_path(@integration) : nil %>

    <div class="alert alert-warning mt-n1">
      Default off. Enable this only if you want Plunk <code>contact.subscribed</code> and <code>contact.unsubscribed</code>
      workflow events to write back into Spree and keep local newsletter consent aligned by email.
    </div>

    <%= preference_field(
      @integration,
      form,
      "unsubscribe_webhook_enabled",
      i18n_scope: "admin.integrations.plunk",
    ) %>
    <p class="mb-4 mt-n2">
      When enabled, configure dedicated Plunk workflow webhooks for <code>contact.subscribed</code> and
      <code>contact.unsubscribed</code> and send both to
      <% if unsubscribe_webhook_path.present? %>
        <code><%= unsubscribe_webhook_path %></code>.
      <% else %>
        the integration-specific webhook URL shown here after you save this connection.
      <% end %>
    </p>

    <%= preference_field(
      @integration,
      form,
      "unsubscribe_webhook_authorization_token",
      i18n_scope: "admin.integrations.plunk",
    ) unless @integration.new_record? %>
    <%= render(
      "spree/admin/integrations/forms/plunk_password_field",
      form: form,
      field: :preferred_unsubscribe_webhook_authorization_token,
      label: Spree.t("unsubscribe_webhook_authorization_token", scope: "admin.integrations.plunk"),
      required: false
    ) if @integration.new_record? %>
    <p class="mb-0 mt-n2">
      Required when the webhook is enabled. Send the same value as an <code>Authorization</code> header in Plunk using
      the format <code>Bearer your-secret-token</code>. The intake only accepts explicit contact subscription-state
      semantics and suppresses local Spree event publication during writeback to avoid immediate echo loops.
    </p>
  </div>
</div>
